{
  "notes": [
    "Q2 menu steps for q2_ui.py drive. Coordinates are client pixels of a 1920x1080 window (the run starts the game WINDOWED SCREENWIDTH=1920 SCREENHEIGHT=1080).",
    "Reference crops: main_menu, sp_menu, setup_start, loading_begin, hud_buttons come from tools/probe_mod/g1_capture/scenes.json (read-only); the others are refs/*.png here, cut from the 2026-10-30 calibration shots (FoC 1.121, English).",
    "Each list ends at the moment the galaxy / battle runs. After that the driver never touches the window, so the traced session gets no player input (the command stream stays empty).",
    "Galactic: the side dropdown and Advanced options are remembered by the game, so the steps set them explicitly (Empire, Medium, Advanced -> Default). Advanced defaults seen: starting credits 10000, tech 3, max tech 5, auto-resolve Ask.",
    "The GC opening shows the 'Active Story Objectives' dialog, which pauses the galaxy; the last galactic step closes it (as the 2026-10-27 manual run did).",
    "Skirmish: Space, map list scrolled to the top, slot 2 = Medium AI (Rebellion, Team 2), (2) Battle Over Geonosis, Advanced -> Default (credits 6000, heroes/free units/superweapons on, win = destroy enemy space station). sk_slots also checks the player name 'Gabriel' / Empire in slot 1, so it is machine-specific. Ends after Begin on the loading screen, once the HUD shows.",
    "The game draws its cursor (which follows the real mouse, not the posted clicks) into the screenshot, so the sk_geonosis crop stops left of the map-name click point [464,460,592,482] (2026-10-30 runs failed at dist 1.5 with the cursor over the full-width crop)."
  ],
  "scenarios": {
